        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Coulee_Dam",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The idea to divert the Columbia River into the Grand Coulee dates back to 1892 when a scheme by Laughlin McLean was reported.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Coulee_Dam",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1941 folk singer Woody Guthrie wrote “The Song of the Grand Coulee Dam” while working there, paid by Bonneville Power Administration.",
